  "title": "Hedetniemi's Conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture If $G,H$ are simple finite graphs, then $\\chi(G \\times H) = \\min \\{ \\chi(G), \\chi(H) \\}$.\n\nHere $G \\times H$ is the tensor product (also called the direct or categorical product) of $G$ and $H$.",
